<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ dollar ends lower, uptrend seen intact.</title>
<headline>NZ dollar ends lower, uptrend seen intact.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand dollar ended lower on Friday but the uptrend was expected to remain intact.</p>
<p>The currency ended at US$0.6990/95 and at 66.58 on the Trade-Weighted Index from 0.7003/10 and 66.67 at the open.</p>
<p>The range on the day was US$0.6988-06.</p>
<p>&quot;If we break 0.7020-25 then we will go up, but at the moment there seems to be reasonable offering interest around 0.7015-20,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>-- James Gray (64 9 302 1253)</p>
</text>
